.IX Title "Clownfish::StringIterator 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::StringIterator 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::StringIterator \- Iterate Unicode code points in a String.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 4
\&    my $iter = $string\->top;
\&    while (my $code_point = $iter\->next) {
\&        ...
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string_iterator\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SS assign
.IX Subsection "assign"
.Vb 1
\&    $string_iterator\->assign($other);
.Ve
.PP
Assign the source string and current position of \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR to \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string_iterator\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one StringIterator is less than, equal to, or
greater than another by comparing their character positions. Throws an
exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is not a StringIterator pointing to the same
source string as \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the StringIterators are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR
is less than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than
\&\f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS has_next
.IX Subsection "has_next"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string_iterator\->has_next();
.Ve
.PP
Return true if the iterator is not at the end of the string.
.SS has_prev
.IX Subsection "has_prev"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string_iterator\->has_prev();
.Ve
.PP
Return true if the iterator is not at the start of the string.
.SS next
.IX Subsection "next"
.Vb 1
\&    my $code_point = $iter\->next;
.Ve
.PP
Return the code point after the current position and advance the
iterator. Returns undef at the end of the string. Returns zero
but true for U+0000.
.SS prev
.IX Subsection "prev"
.Vb 1
\&    my $code_point = $iter\->prev;
.Ve
.PP
Return the code point before the current position and go one step back.
Returns undef at the start of the string. Returns zero but true for
U+0000.
.SS advance
.IX Subsection "advance"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string_iterator\->advance($num);
.Ve
.PP
Skip code points.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBnum\fR \- The number of code points to skip.
.PP
Returns: the number of code points actually skipped. This can be less
than the requested number if the end of the string is reached.
.SS recede
.IX Subsection "recede"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string_iterator\->recede($num);
.Ve
.PP
Skip code points backward.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBnum\fR \- The number of code points to skip.
.PP
Returns: the number of code points actually skipped. This can be less
than the requested number if the start of the string is reached.
.SS skip_whitespace
.IX Subsection "skip_whitespace"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string_iterator\->skip_whitespace();
.Ve
.PP
Skip whitespace.  Whitespace is any character that has the Unicode
property \f(CW\*(C`White_Space\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Returns: the number of code points skipped.
.SS skip_whitespace_back
.IX Subsection "skip_whitespace_back"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string_iterator\->skip_whitespace_back();
.Ve
.PP
Skip whitespace backward.  Whitespace is any character that has the
Unicode property \f(CW\*(C`White_Space\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Returns: the number of code points skipped.
.SS starts_with
.IX Subsection "starts_with"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string_iterator\->starts_with($prefix);
.Ve
.PP
Test whether the content after the iterator starts with \f(CW\*(C`prefix\*(C'\fR.
.SS ends_with
.IX Subsection "ends_with"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string_iterator\->ends_with($suffix);
.Ve
.PP
Test whether the content before the iterator ends with \f(CW\*(C`suffix\*(C'\fR.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::StringIterator isa Clownfish::Obj.
